  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The gender of names",
   "texto": [
    "It's almost always known from the last letter. It ends in **consonante**: masculine (студент, врач, дом). It ends in **-а** or **-я**: feminine (студентка, машина, семья). It ends in **-о** or **-е**: neutral (окно, море).",
    "The grammatical genre does not always match that of the person. **Врач** and **инженер** are masculine-shaped, but may refer to a woman: **Наташа — врач**, **Лаура — инженер**. In Spanish, it is said «medical» and «ingeniera».",
    "The pronouns are **он** (it), **она** (it) and **оно** (it)."
